  "final_text": "The space and the alert rule are created, and the rule is enabled and running.\n\n- **Space:** `e2e-haiku-93010840`. I gave it the display name `e2e-haiku-93010840` because no other name was specified.\n- **Rule:** \"E2E e7190504 flight watch\" (id `2f2ad266-157c-49c3-8dd1-ab6eb3c3dad1`), type `.es-query`, consumer `stackAlerts`.\n- **Condition:** fires when the count is greater than 0 over a 5-minute window on `kibana_sample_data_flights`, using `timestamp` as the time field.\n- **Query:** `match_all`, since you didn't specify a filter. The rule therefore fires whenever the window contains any flight document.\n- **Schedule:** I used a 1-minute check interval. You didn't specify one, so tell me if you want a different value.\n- **Actions:** none attached, so the rule will track alerts but not send notifications.\n\nI read the rule back after enabling it and confirmed `enabled: true` and the params above.",
